  "description": "The unit tests beside the code, run with `cargo test -p agent-fs` in macos/rust. uring.rs tests and test_retry_without_noatime are compiled only on Linux; aio.rs has no tests of its own and is exercised on macOS through fsio's load_many tests.",
  "entities": [
    {
      "id": "read-unchanged-and-diff",
      "title": "Read: unchanged, diff, ranges and caps",
      "summary": "Repeats are markers, changed files are hunks, and ranges, caps and errors behave as documented.",
      "subject": [
        { "path": "macos/rust/agent-fs/src/.dev/feature.json", "entityId": "unchanged-replies" },
        { "path": "macos/rust/agent-fs/src/.dev/feature.json", "entityId": "diff-replies" },
        { "path": "macos/rust/agent-fs/src/.dev/feature.json", "entityId": "bounded-output" },
        { "path": "macos/rust/agent-fs/src/.dev/operation.json", "entityId": "read" }
      ],
      "criteria": [
        "A second identical read sends no content and a changed read sends only a diff",
        "Ranges, truncation and if_none_match behave as documented",
        "Once a file is old enough to trust its stamp, repeats are answered without reloading it",
        "A diff that is not smaller than the file falls back to full content",
        "Binary files, long lines and byte caps are reported in the reply",
        "Reads fail on directories and missing files, and reject bad ranges"
      ],
      "checks": [
        { "type": "automated", "path": "macos/rust/agent-fs/src/engine.rs", "symbol": "tests::test_read_unchanged_then_diff", "command": "cargo test -p agent-fs" },
